<title>ITALY: Italy opens up foreign currency repos.</title>
<headline>Italy opens up foreign currency repos.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said on Tuesday it was opening up foreign currency repo tenders from November 1 to all banks and brokerages with assets of more than 50 billion lire.</p>
<p>Previously, only a specialist tier of participants had been allowed to take part in those tenders.</p>
<p>The central bank said in a statement, however, that repo tenders in lire would continue to be open only to specialist participants.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
